Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} until it uncurls by spending an action (this action has the move trait).</p>"},"rules":[{"key":"RollOption","label":"Curled Up","domain":"all","option":"curlUp","toggleable":true,"value":false},{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":"ac","value":2,"predicate":["curlUp"],"roll-options":["all"]}],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"1yfdxvh4L8PNpbII","name":"Spew Shale","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The shale charger spews forth a frothy mix of scree and mud in a @Template[type:cone|distance:20], dealing [[/r 4d6[piercing]]] damage (@Check[type:reflex|dc:23|name:Spew Shale DC|traits:damaging-effect, earth, evocation, primal|showDC:gm]{basic Reflex} save). Creatures who critically fail their saving throw are also @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.TkIyaNPgTZFBCCuh]{Dazzled} for 1 minute.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["earth","primal"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"action"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":2},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"zY2sDQBKtgLfzEH9","name":"Tunneling Charge","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The shale charger Strides in a straight line up to twice its burrow Speed, charging through creatures and loose gravel alike. The charger's movement can be any combination of moving on land and burrowing, and it can move through the spaces of any creatures in its path. When the charger moves through the space of a Large or smaller creature, the creature must attempt a @Check[type:reflex|dc:24|name:Tunneling Charge DC|traits:damaging-effect|showDC:gm]{Reflex} save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes [[/r 3d6[bludgeoning]]] damage and is knocked aside; the creature chooses an adjacent space and Steps there.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes [[/r 5d6[bludgeoning]]] damage and is knocked @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.j91X7x0XSomq8d60]{Prone}.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes [[/r 7d6[piercing]]] damage and is pushed in a straight line along the shale charger's path. The creature stops moving at the end of the shale charger's Stride.</p>\n"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"action"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":2},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"La57XISD2unXrQoG","name":"Rock Stride","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":-100000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A shale charger ignores difficult terrain caused in caves and rocky mountains.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"yyvzxCjCCMnJ2C4z","name":"Rock Tunneler","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":-50000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A shale charger can burrow through solid stone at a Speed of 15 feet, leaving behind a tunnel.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"OXb9KPNmHu6svgoG","name":"Horn","type":"melee","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"value":"","gm":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":["deadly-d8"],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"rmxbqrx06hpqaqnfybhw":{"damage":"2d8+8","damageType":"piercing","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":17},"attackEffects":{"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"dvGspGr3HdLGDbY3","name":"Rock","type":"melee","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"value":"","gm":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":["range-increment-60"],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"lrpijqtub7od3f1zdtbv":{"damage":"2d4+8","damageType":"bludgeoning","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":16},"attackEffects":{"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}}],"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"pf2e":{"lootable":false},"core":{}},"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":100,"temp":0,"max":100,"details":""},"ac":{"value":24,"details":"26 while curled up","base":24},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":40,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"burrow","label":"Burrow","value":30}],"details":"rock stride"},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed"}],"resistances":[{"type":"piercing","value":5},{"type":"slashing","value":5}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":6},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Shale chargers are an extraordinarily large subspecies of shale spitter. Unlike their more sedentary cousins, shale chargers take a far more active role in their pack's ever-expanding search for new mineral deposits. Rushing forth on its cascading rows of legs and slamming its reinforced chitinous plating into anything in its path, the shale charger silently demands anyone opposing it to stand aside—and it doesn't ask twice.</p>\n<p>Chargers can burrow at great speed, rapidly digging through even solid rock and opening up new tunnels for their smaller comrades to explore. Whereas the more common shale spitter might embed itself in an area and spend months or even years scouring a single cavern for minerals, a shale charger essentially feeds as it goes. Its simple digestive system sorts soil and sand from its nutrient-rich content as quickly as it can churn through the earth.</p>\n<p>Dwarven spelunkers and other explorers of the subterranean world rejoice at finding shale charger droppings. Where there's a shale charger, riches are sure to abound, so the thinking goes—assuming you don't first find yourself going down the wrong direction a charger's one-way tunnel.</p>\n<h2>Of Horns and Egos</h2>\n<p>Shale chargers grow hard, jagged horns atop their skulls, which aid them in both fighting as well as digging. When two shale chargers meet, the two are prone to joust for days on end, heedless of any other creatures around them. It's not uncommon for the winner of such jousts to achieve victory by snapping off the horn of its opponent. While its broken horn regrows over a course of months, a defeated shale charger is considerably more subdued, even skittish. Wounded shale chargers offer more than enough proof that these animals can feel emotions such as pride as well as humiliation.</p>\n<h2>Shale Spitter</h2>\n<p>Earthen isopods that subsist on crystals and stones in order to proliferate under mighty mountains, shale spitters run the gamut in terms of the challenges they pose to spelunking adventurers. The lowliest of shale spitter kind are little more than scuttling nuisances or, at worst, swarms of stony spawn. On the other end of the spectrum are behemoths that might be called mountains in themselves—looming terrors that dominate entire caverns and give form to whole underground ecosystems. All share one common characteristic that makes every shale spitter highly sought after by fortune-seeking monster hunters: Their crystalline waste matter is literally worth more than its weight in gold.</p>\n<h2>Monster Part Subsystem</h2>\n<p><strong>Shale Charger Creature 6 </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 30/65/125 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (heavy), shield, perception item, skill items (Athletics, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, energy resistant (positive), sensory (darkvision), strength, sturdy, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary","authors":"Brant Vallier","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":-4},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":0}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":13,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":14},"stealth":{"base":13,"special":[{"label":"in caves","base":17,"predicate":["terrain:cave"]}]}},"traits":{"value":["animal","earth"],"rarity":"common","size":{"value":"lg"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"prototypeToken":{"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":true}},"height":2,"width":2,"disposition":-1,"name":"Shale Charger","actorLink":false,"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"bar2":{"attribute":null},"randomImg":false,"light":{"alpha":0.25,"angle":360,"bright":0,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"speed":5,"intensity":5,"type":null,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"color":null,"attenuation":0.5,"negative":false,"priority":0},"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e/art/Tokens/shale_charger.webp","tint":"#ffffff","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"sight":{"angle":360,"enabled":false,"range":0,"brightness":1,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e/art/Subjects/shale_charger.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":2},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"6.1.0","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1663517316870,"modifiedTime":1729379234252,"lastModifiedBy":"ZdvNMqfYMlbFrAL2","compendiumSource":"Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e.pf2e-battlezoo-bestiary.Actor.XcnEq7zBQm91hFXS","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}}